Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 20:24:39 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] Let the relocated right-panel tests run against a DOM

Renaming these four into the collected tree made the runner pick them up,
but they kept the project default of `environment: "node"`. Every one of
them renders through React Testing Library, so three failed outright and
RoomSearchJumpToDate took a worker thread down with it: an unhandled
rejection during module init is fatal to the whole thread rather than to
the test, which silently drops the file from both the pass and fail
tallies. Opting each file into happy-dom is the same per-file convention
every other component test here already follows.

The path-rewriting pass that repointed the relative imports also caught
two strings it should not have. It rewrote a CSS class selector as though
it were a module path, which happy-dom rejects outright where jsdom would
have quietly returned nothing, and it left the module mock naming the old
module while the import moved to the new one, so the mock stopped
intercepting anything.
